Synthesis methodology
=====================

In order to run a toplevel compile of the MPMC, the lower levels
(MpmcCore and MpmcTIC) are compiled separately at their target frequencies
(156 MHz and 10 MHz respectively).

The Mpmc toplevel compile can be done only if the required dbs of MpmcCore and
MpmcTIC are made available in ./db by compiling them separately first using the
'MpmcCore.cmd' and 'MpmcTIC.cmd' scripts and then using the toplevel compile
script 'Mpmc.cmd'.

The TEST_METH variable should not be set to 'scaninsert' for the MpmcCore and
MpmcTIC compiles. In order to create a fully routed scan netlist of the MPMC,
the MpmcCore and MpmcTIC are to be compiled with the TEST_METH variable set to
'scanready'. The TEST_METH variable is set to 'scaninsert' only during the
toplevel compile of Mpmc. These changes will be made by the makefile during
scaninsert synthesis.

Synthesis script files
======================

Top level, Mpmc, synthesis files
--------------------------------
Mpmc.cmd : Top level synthesis command file
Mpmc.scr : Top level constraints file
Mpmc_exceptions.scr : Top level exceptions file
Mpmc_scan.cmd : Top level scan insertion file

MpmcCore sub-block synthesis files
----------------------------------
MpmcCore.cmd : MpmcCore synthesis command file
MpmcCore.scr : MpmcCore constraints file
MpmcCore_exceptions.scr : Mpmc exceptions file

MpmcTIC sub-block synthesis files
---------------------------------
MpmcTIC.cmd : MpmcTIC synthesis command file
MpmcTIC.scr : MpmcTIC constraints file


